==Afrikaans==
===Etymology===
From {{etyl|nl|af}} {{term|boer|lang=nl}} (noun) and {{term|boeren|lang=nl}} (verb).
===Noun===
{{af-noun|boere|boertjie}}

# {{l|en|farmer}}; [[peasant]]
# {{context|chess|lang=af}} [[pawn]]; least valuable piece in chess

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|chess piece}} {{l|af|pion}}

===Verb===
{{af-verb}}

# to [[farm]]
# to continuously encounter someone at a specific place
#: {{usex|lang=af|Hy '''boer''' daar by haar huis.|t=He '''is always there''' at her house.}}
# to [[stay]]; to [[sojourn]]; to [[linger]]
#: {{usex|lang=af|Hy't die heel middag by daardie meisie '''geboer'''.|t=He '''stayed over''' at that girl['s place] the whole afternoon.}}
#: {{usex|lang=af|Moenie op 'n vraag '''boer''' nie.|t=Don't '''linger''' on a question.}}

